        "content": "Documents give contradicting answers about the same thing. Other documents, which take no side, may state a fact that makes one of the answers impossible.\n\nQuestion: What is the population of Kaliganj Upazila according to the 1991 Bangladesh census?\n\nAnswer A: 219,126\n  about: Kaliganj Upazila 1991 Bangladesh census\n  sense: population\n  as of: 1991\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 2\n  evidence: \"As of the 1991 Bangladesh census, Kaliganj had a population of 219,126.\" [document 1]; \"As of the 1991 Bangladesh census , Kaliganj had a population of 219,126 .\" [document 2]\n\nAnswer B: 175915\n  about: Kaliganj Upazila 1991 Bangladesh census\n  sense: population\n  as of: 1991\n  kind: factual\n  independent sources: 3\n  evidence: \"As of the 1991 Bangladesh census, Kaliganj has a population of 175915.\" [document 4]; \"\"As of the 1991 Bangladesh census , Kaliganj has a population of 175915 .\"\" [document 5]; \"As of the 1991 Bangladesh census , Kaliganj has a population of 175915 .\" [document 6]\n\nThe other documents:\nDocument 3: and Christians 0.09%. Kaliganj had a literacy rate of 51.78% for the population 7 years and above. According to the 1991 Bangladesh census, Kaliganj had a population of 225,596. Males constituted 50.7% of the population, and females 49.3%. The population aged 18 or over was 115,458. Kaliganj had an average literacy rate of 32.3% (7+ years), compared to the national average of 32.4%. Kaliganj has 12 Unions/Wards, 244 Mauzas/Mahallas, and 256 villages. Women Vice Chairman : Vice Chairman : Sayeed Mehedi (from Awami League) Upazila Nirbahi Officer (UNO) : Mohammad Toufiq-e-Elahi Chowdhury DR. A.K.M. ASADUZZAMAN: Pediatrician. The Kakshiyali River (actually\n\nLook in the other documents for a fact that rules one answer out: a date of birth that makes a person too young, for example, or a plain statement that the answer is false. Use only what these documents say, nothing you know from elsewhere. A fact that only makes an answer less likely does not count.\n\nReply with JSON only. If such a fact is there:\n{\"reason\": \"one sentence\", \"impossible\": \"A\", \"document\": 1, \"quote\": \"\"}\n\"impossible\" is the letter of the answer that is ruled out. \"quote\" is the sentence stating the fact, copied word for word, and \"document\" is the number of the document it is in.\nIf there is none:\n{\"impossible\": null}\n\nInside a JSON string, write a double quote as \\\"."
